@startuml catalogue-cors-preflight
title Gym catalogue: OPTIONS preflight

actor Browser
participant "CatalogueWorker" as Worker
participant "Router" as Router
participant "Cors" as Cors

== Allow-listed Origin ==
Browser -> Worker : OPTIONS /exercises\nOrigin: http://localhost:5173\nAccess-Control-Request-Method: GET
Worker -> Router : route(request)
Router -> Cors : preflightResponse(request, origins)
note right of Cors
  Origin is on the allow list
  parsed from ALLOWED_ORIGINS.
end note
Cors --> Router : 204 No Content\naccess-control-allow-origin: http://localhost:5173\naccess-control-allow-methods: GET, OPTIONS\naccess-control-allow-headers: content-type\naccess-control-max-age: 600\nvary: Origin
Router --> Worker : Response
Worker --> Browser : 204

== Disallowed Origin ==
Browser -> Worker : OPTIONS /exercises\nOrigin: https://attacker.example
Worker -> Router : route(request)
Router -> Cors : preflightResponse(request, origins)
note right of Cors
  Origin not on allow list.
  No CORS headers returned;
  the browser blocks the real request.
end note
Cors --> Router : 204 No Content\n(no CORS headers)
Router --> Worker : Response
Worker --> Browser : 204 (browser blocks follow-up)

@enduml
